      ":question/problem": "The value $V(t)$ of a tech device varies according to the differential equation ${V}^{\u2032}(t)=-rV(t),$ where $t$ is the time, measured in years, and $r>0.$ It is known that the value reduces by one-half after the first year. How long does it take for the value to reduce to one-fifth of its original value? Round your answer to one decimal place."
